Only raw frame bytes are reproduced (as test fixtures), not goosestalker's own
Python/Scapy source, none of which was read or ported. The implementation
under test (`goose.zig`'s header/extension/MAC logic) is the authors' own,
modelled from public descriptions of IEC 62351-6 as `SPEC.md` already
documents; these captures anchor the frame *header* (EtherType/APPID/Length/
Reserved fields) and the APDU/extension boundary against genuine wire bytes,
not the security extension itself, which no surveyed real-world capture
carries. `src/goose_capture_test.zig`'s doc comment explains the scope in
full, and additionally uses this module's own `ber.zig` TLV reader to decode
the real `goosePdu` fields (`gocbRef`/`stNum`/`sqNum`/`allData`) as a bonus
anchor of that shared primitive — `goose.zig` itself never interprets those
fields (see its module doc comment); their semantic model belongs to the
sibling `iec61850` module, not this one.
